[95.816391, "o", "# Edge Gateway Event Loop Bug Fix\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\nHTTP health endpoint at localhost:8080/health would hang indefinitely when mosquitto MQTT broker was running, but respond immediately when mosquitto was killed.\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\nThe original code had an event loop management bug:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef main():\r\n    loop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\r\n    asyncio.set_event_loop(loop)\r\n    loop.create_task(mqtt_loop())  # Task created in this loop\r\n    \r\n    app = create_app()\r\n    web.run_app(app, ...)  # Creates its OWN new event loop internally!\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe MQTT client task was running in one event loop, while web.run_app() created a separate event loop for the HTTP server. This caused the HTTP handlers to hang when trying to check the MQTT client status across event loops.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nUse aiohttp's application lifecycle hooks (on_startup) to ensure both MQTT and HTTP run in the same event loop:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nasync def start_mqtt(app):\r\n    app['mqtt_task'] = asyncio.create_task(mqtt_loop())\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    a"]
[95.81645, "o", "pp = create_app()\r\n    app.on_startup.append(start_mqtt)  # MQTT task created in web.run_app's loop\r\n    app.on_cleanup.append(cleanup_mqtt)\r\n    web.run_app(app, host='0.0.0.0', port=8080, ...)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n- Health endpoint responds instantly: ✓\r\n- MQTT connection maintained: ✓\r\n- Sensor data publishing works: ✓\r\n- Ready for deployment to 200 gateway fleet\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n```bash\r\n./start.sh &\r\ncurl http://localhost:8080/health\r\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/sensor -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"test\": \"data\"}'\r\n```\r\n"]
